---
import { WEATHER_PLACEHOLDER } from "../utils/weather";

interface Props {
  /** Place the crawler is configured for; see the `cron` worker's wrangler config. */
  location?: string;
}

const { location = "根室市" } = Astro.props;
---

<!--
  A reading, not a dashboard. It sits in the margin of the index as a daisyUI
  `card`, so it is only ever as wide as its column and never competes with the
  writing. The reading is the library's `stat`, which is the shape for a number
  and what it means; the essentials come first and the full set of readings
  follows the hairline for the reader who wants them. The snapshot is crawled
  every ten minutes and served from object storage, so it is filled in by
  `enhanceWeatherWidget` rather than at build time.

  daisyUI's `stat-title` and `stat-desc` ship at 60% ink, which is under this
  site's AA floor, so both carry the named `--ink-muted` tier instead.

  The card spans the rail's width, as the archive card beneath it does, and its
  height is the height of its content: it holds a reading, and when the crawl has
  not come back the only honest height is the height of the sentence that says
  so, rather than a bordered void stretched to the column.
-->
<section
  class="card border-base-300 border"
  data-weather
  tabindex="-1"
  aria-labelledby="weather-heading"
>
  <div class="card-body gap-0 p-0">
    <div class="border-base-300 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b px-5 py-3">
      <h2 id="weather-heading" class="label">
        天気
      </h2>
      <span class="data">{location}</span>
    </div>

    <div class="px-5 py-5" aria-live="polite" data-weather-live>
      <!--
        The skeleton belongs to the script, not to the page. It used to be drawn
        from the first paint and hidden by the script once the crawl answered,
        which meant a browser without scripting shimmered here for as long as the
        tab stayed open: a placeholder for work nothing was going to do.

        Revealed by `load()` now, the same way the loader is revealed by the head
        script, so it is only ever shown to a browser that can also take it away.
      -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4" data-weather-loading hidden>
        <div class="skeleton size-10 shrink-0"></div>
        <div class="w-full space-y-2">
          <div class="skeleton h-7 w-24"></div>
          <div class="skeleton h-3 w-32"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="data" data-weather-error hidden></p>

      <div data-weather-content hidden>
        <div class="stat p-0">
          <div class="stat-figure size-10" data-weather-icon></div>
          <div class="stat-value text-3xl" data-weather-temp>
            {WEATHER_PLACEHOLDER}
          </div>
          <div
            class="stat-desc text-[color:var(--ink-muted)]"
            data-weather-description
          >
            {WEATHER_PLACEHOLDER}
          </div>
          <div
            class="stat-desc text-[color:var(--ink-muted)]"
            data-weather-feels-like
            hidden
          ></div>
        </div>

        <p class="data mt-4" hidden data-weather-updated>
          更新 <time data-weather-observed></time>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!--
      What a reader without scripting gets. The reading is fetched from the
      crawler's object at request time and cannot be baked into the page, so the
      honest thing to say is that it is not there rather than to leave an empty
      card.
    -->
    <noscript>
      <p class="data px-5 text-pretty">
        天気は JavaScript を有効にすると表示されます。
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <!--
      The way out of a failed or empty reading. Both are answered by the same
      action: the snapshot is a file the crawler rewrites every ten minutes, so
      asking again is the whole of what a reader can do about it.

      It sits outside the live region on purpose. Inside it, the button would be
      announced as part of the reading it is meant to be a response to.
    -->
    <button
      type="button"
      class="btn btn-sm mx-5 mb-5 min-h-11 self-start"
      data-weather-retry
      hidden
    >
      再読み込み
    </button>
  </div>

  <!--
    The full reading is a large-screen affordance, so the wrapper hides it below
    the break the way the `hidden` attribute hides an empty one, and the two do
    not fight: the attribute is on the reading, the breakpoint is on the wrapper.
  -->
  <div class="hidden lg:block">
    <div class="border-base-300 border-t px-5 py-4" data-weather-report hidden>
      <h3 class="label mb-3">詳細</h3>
      <dl class="list gap-1 p-0" data-weather-details></dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <template data-weather-detail-template>
    <div class="list-row p-0">
      <dt class="text-[color:var(--ink-muted)] text-sm"></dt>
      <dd
        class="text-right text-sm font-medium"
        style="font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums"
      ></dd>
    </div>
  </template>
</section>

<script>
  import { enhanceWeatherWidget } from "../scripts/weather-widget";

  enhanceWeatherWidget();
</script>
